WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.480
If you only have $100 and a full-time job, you&nbsp;
need to swing trade. But you can't just guess.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:14.080
You need a mechanical system. This is my complete&nbsp;
swing trading strategy. And it does exactly three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:20.800
things. It uses two specific moving averages to&nbsp;
trap price inside a high probability pullback&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:27.840
zone. It gives you a yes or no entry trigger&nbsp;
using one exact pattern and it uses a mechanical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:34.520
exit framework that locks in profit early. Look at&nbsp;
what happens when you combine these three things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:40.600
This is a three-hour trade on gold caught&nbsp;
with zero emotion using the exact rules you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:46.720
are about to learn. This is how the engine&nbsp;
works. You buy pullbacks inside uptrends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:54.720
and you short pullbacks inside downtrends. That is&nbsp;
the entire swing trading game. Price climbs, dips,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:02.960
climbs, then dips again. Each of those dips inside&nbsp;
the climb is your entry window. Now flip it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:10.280
Price drops, bounces into the trend, drops,&nbsp;
bounces again. Every bounce is a short window.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:16.880
Markets spend roughly half their time trending&nbsp;
or pulling back inside trends. We will use the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:23.680
daily time frame only. This is non-negotiable.&nbsp;
Lower charts are noise factories that punish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:30.280
small accounts with fees and bad fills. The&nbsp;
daily forces patience. You look for the setup&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:37.200
after dinner or in the morning. You make one call&nbsp;
and you close the laptop. That's the whole frame.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:44.600
Now, defining the swing trading game handles the&nbsp;
what. It does not tell you which charts qualify,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:51.080
which is the only thing that matters. Next, you&nbsp;
need two exponential moving averages. Find them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.080 --> 00:02:00.320
in Trading View. Set period 20 on the first one,&nbsp;
period 50 on the second, both close, both daily.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:07.800
Why these two, the 20 tracks short-term momentum,&nbsp;
the level swing traders are reacting to today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:16.680
the 50 tracks longerterm institutional drift. When&nbsp;
both agree, real money agrees. When they disagree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:24.480
you have noise pretending to be a trend. Three&nbsp;
checks in this exact order. Alignment, slope,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:32.840
and price position. The 20 must sit above the&nbsp;
54 longs, below for shorts. Both moving averages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:40.480
must point in the same direction. And price has&nbsp;
to be on the right side of both. Above for longs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:49.240
below for shorts. Look at this. The 20 sits above&nbsp;
the 50. Both lines pointing up at a clean angle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:56.680
Price stacked on top of both. That's&nbsp;
a tradable uptrend. Now mirror it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:04.320
The 20 sits below the 50. Both pointing&nbsp;
down. Price below both. Tradable downtrend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:12.160
Now look at this one. The lines are tangled&nbsp;
together, crossing back and forth. No clear order.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:19.480
You close the chart when you see this. And&nbsp;
this one, the lines are aligned but flat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:26.640
No slope. Price just drifting sideways. Again,&nbsp;
close the chart. You have no reason to trade.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:34.920
Remember this. Moving averages don't fail in&nbsp;
trends. They fail in chop. The slope filter alone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:42.160
kills roughly 50% of the garbage setups before you&nbsp;
even look for an entry trigger. That is why this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:48.000
filter exists to stop you taking trades that&nbsp;
were never going to work in the first place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:55.040
So hard rule, if the EMAs are aligned and&nbsp;
sloping clean, you have a tradable context.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.560 --> 00:04:02.920
If lines are tangled, flat, or crossing, skip&nbsp;
the chart and don't reopen it that day. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:09.840
trend filter is the easy half. The next layer is&nbsp;
what turns a trending chart into an actual setup.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:17.160
A trend alone is not enough. If you buy after&nbsp;
price has already moved far above the two lines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:23.320
you are late. You need price to come back into&nbsp;
value. That is what the pullback gives you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:30.840
In an uptrend, a pullback happens when early&nbsp;
buyers take profit, short-term traders get scared,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:37.120
and price drifts back down. But if the trend is&nbsp;
still healthy, stronger buyers often use that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:45.160
weakness to enter. So, we need a pullback zone,&nbsp;
not a random area, a defined zone for our setup.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:51.920
The pullback zone is the area between the 20&nbsp;
and the 50. That is where price must pull back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:59.200
before we even care about an entry. Why a zone,&nbsp;
you might ask? Because price rarely respects one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:07.320
perfect line. Sometimes it touches the 20 line and&nbsp;
reacts. Sometimes it pushes deeper toward the 50.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:14.640
Sometimes it trades between both for a few candles&nbsp;
before continuing. If you use one exact line, you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:22.080
will miss good trades and force bad ones. A zone&nbsp;
matches how markets actually move. Look at this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:30.600
Price is in an uptrend. The 20 line is above the&nbsp;
51. Price pulls back into the space between them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:38.720
That is the zone. Now the chart has our&nbsp;
attention. Now here, same thing. Clean downtrend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:44.960
pull back into the zone. Price is not to extend&nbsp;
it anymore. This is where we start looking for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:53.480
short trigger. If price closes beyond the 50 EMA&nbsp;
on a daily candle, the setup is dead. No entry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.480 --> 00:06:01.120
no second chance, no waiting for it to come back.&nbsp;
Move to the next chart. So, binary rule, price&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:09.760
inside the band with the trend intact. Setup is&nbsp;
alive. Price closed beyond the 50. Setup is dead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:18.080
Okay. Trend is intact. Price is in the zone. Now&nbsp;
we wait for one specific signal and only one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:25.920
The entry trigger is the outside bar. An outside&nbsp;
bar is a candle whose full body covers the full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:33.720
body of the candle before it. It must dominate the&nbsp;
body of the prior candle. In an uptrend pullback,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:39.520
you want the outside bar to close bullish. That&nbsp;
means it closes in the direction of the trend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:46.840
In a downtrend pullback, you want it to close&nbsp;
bearish again in the direction of the trend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:52.520
This candle matters because it shows a shift&nbsp;
in control. That tells you the pullback may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.520 --> 00:07:00.320
be ending. Pay attention here. Trend is up. Price&nbsp;
pulls into the zone. This candle breaks the high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:09.240
and low of the previous candle and closes green.&nbsp;
Valid outside bar. Now this one downtrend. Price&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:15.640
pulls back into the zone. The candle breaks above&nbsp;
and below the previous candle and closes red.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:23.960
Valid short trigger. Now look at this third chart.&nbsp;
This is an outside bar, but it forms far above the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:31.560
pullback zone. It is tempting, but you skip this.&nbsp;
The candle is valid, but the location is wrong.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:38.480
And the setup needs both. Now look at this one.&nbsp;
This candle looks strong, but it does not break&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:46.640
both the previous high and the previous low. So&nbsp;
it is not an outside bar. You skip this, too. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:52.880
outside bar is the market telling you the pullback&nbsp;
has resolved. You do not enter before it forms.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:59.760
Entry is always on the close of the outside&nbsp;
bar. You wait for the daily candle to close.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:06.720
If the candle meets the rule, you enter. If it&nbsp;
does not, you do nothing. Okay, now you are in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:13.240
the trade. Most swing trading guides end here.&nbsp;
But this is actually where the work begins because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:20.200
where you exit determines whether this system&nbsp;
makes money. You're in a long trade right here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:27.560
After all conditions were met, the stop goes just&nbsp;
beyond the opposite extreme of the outside bar.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:34.760
This candle defines your entry and it also defines&nbsp;
your risk. If price breaks the opposite side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:42.720
of that candle, the trigger failed. Now we use&nbsp;
a three tier exit. Tier one is the one R. Once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:50.000
price moves in your favor by the same distance&nbsp;
as your risk, you take off 50% of the position.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:57.320
This is mechanical and the reason is simple. Small&nbsp;
accounts need emotional protection. When you take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:06.680
50% off at 1 R, you lock in a real win early. Tier&nbsp;
2 is the break even shift. After 1 R is hit, move&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:14.480
the stop on the remaining 50% to your entry price.&nbsp;
Now the trade can no longer lose money. The worst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:22.000
case is that the second half comes back and stops&nbsp;
at break even. Third tier is the trailing stop. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:28.960
trail it using swing structure. For a long trade,&nbsp;
trail the stop under the most recent swing low.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:36.160
For a short above the most recent swing high&nbsp;
and only update it after confirmed daily candle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:42.720
closes, not during the candle. This keeps you&nbsp;
in the move until structure actually breaks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:50.720
Look here. Price is in an uptrend and it pulls&nbsp;
into the 20 and 50 zone. A bullish outside bar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:58.800
forms. Entry is on the close. The stop goes under&nbsp;
the outside bar low. After price moves one risk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:07.200
unit in profit, we take 50% off. Then the stop on&nbsp;
the rest moves to break even. After that, as price&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:15.400
continues higher, we trail under each confirmed&nbsp;
swing low. This exit is asymmetric on purpose.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:22.360
Tier one creates a high feelood rate. Tier two&nbsp;
removes downside. Tier three gives the trade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:29.760
a chance to become large. Most traders only do&nbsp;
one of these. You are different. Now imagine it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:37.400
is Monday morning. You have a full-time job. You&nbsp;
do not have 3 hours. You have 20 minutes. So you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:44.480
open your watch list and run the same process&nbsp;
on every chart trend zone trigger and action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:52.880
spy daily. The moving averages are tangled&nbsp;
flat for the last 3 weeks with no slope.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.880 --> 00:11:01.200
Trend test fails on check too. You close the&nbsp;
chart. Euro dollar daily 20 above 50. both sloping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:10.480
up clean and price riding well above both trend&nbsp;
confirmed but price is extended way above the 20&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:18.600
nowhere near the zone no pullback yet so no setup&nbsp;
you keep this one on the watch list for next days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:27.960
then NAS daily strong downtrend the two lines&nbsp;
aligned and sloping down price has bounced up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:36.200
and is sitting right inside the and between the 20&nbsp;
and 50. Yesterday's candle is a small red candle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:44.720
but no outside bar. This one goes on the watch&nbsp;
list. Now gold uptrend is confirmed. Alignment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:51.960
is clean. Price dropped right into the zone and&nbsp;
yesterday's candle closed a bullish outside bar.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.560 --> 00:12:00.120
This is the trade. Stop one tick below the&nbsp;
outside bar low. First partial alert set at one R&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:08.040
break even of an order ready at that level. Three&nbsp;
out of four charts produce no action. That is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:15.160
the goal. Most days you do nothing. Boredom is&nbsp;
the price you pay to grow your small account.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:22.480
Most charts get rejected. Some go to the watch&nbsp;
list and only a few trigger. Some winners run.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:28.960
Some valid trades still lose. This is what&nbsp;
trading actually looks like. But if you want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:35.840
bulletproof your entries, the next layer is adding&nbsp;
key levels, support and resistance. This single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:44.560
filter is the difference between a 50% and a 65%&nbsp;
win rate on the exact same setups. That's the next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:51.200
video. And this is exactly the kind of setup we&nbsp;
break down inside our academy. See you inside.

